From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:30:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/18] lcms2: Add an abort check for building transforms.

cmsSetAbortCheck() sets a process wide callback that is asked while a
transform is built: every 1024 grid points when a CLUT is resampled and
every 64 points when a tone curve is reversed. When it returns TRUE
that step fails, so the build either fails or ends without that
optimization; the caller must then discard the transform. Without a
callback nothing changes.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 thirdparty/lcms2/include/lcms2mt.h    |  9 +++++++++
 thirdparty/lcms2/src/cmserr.c         | 12 ++++++++++++
 thirdparty/lcms2/src/cmsgamma.c       |  5 +++++
 thirdparty/lcms2/src/cmslut.c         |  6 ++++++
 thirdparty/lcms2/src/lcms2_internal.h |  3 +++
 5 files changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/thirdparty/lcms2/include/lcms2mt.h b/thirdparty/lcms2/include/lcms2mt.h
